module

public import Mathlib

/-!
# Mike's Monster table (`irreps_sum.tsv`), checked line by line (R15·L1)

Beth linked `meta-introspector/monster/irreps_sum.tsv` in her Round 15 doc. Each of its 194 rows
takes one irreducible representation of the Monster group (row `i` is entry `i + 1` of OEIS
A001379, the list of their dimensions, counted from 0) and writes its dimension as a product of
powers of the 15 primes that divide the Monster's order, plus the sum of those exponents.

Here the table is copied in as data and checked:

* every row's prime powers multiply back to the OEIS dimension;
* every row's last column is the sum of its exponents;
* the rows are sorted by that sum, largest first;
* the squares of the 194 dimensions add up to the order of the Monster.

The last fact is what character theory predicts (for any finite group, the squares of the
irreducible dimensions add up to the group's order). Here it is checked as arithmetic on the
listed numbers; this file does not build the Monster group or prove the character theory.
-/

